 # Working notes: 5a6c8785f6d9
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Repair `review-de6fb3d52a32cf07`
+
+The pre-repair v1.3.0 sampler chose marker counts independently. Preserved seed 7 produced counts 4/4/4 for the three demonstrations and 3 for the query, so protected Racket confirmed that `always upscale by four` fit every visible example yet changed 15 query cells. The exact source-bound case is `checks/5a6c8785f6d9-pre-repair-case/case.json`; the old source is preserved beside it under `counterexamples/review-de6fb3d52a32cf07/`.
+
+Version 2.0.1 replaces the random lesson counts with a deterministic 2/3/4/4 four-slot curriculum. Every three-example rotation contains at least two scale factors and at least one factor-4 witness, which rejects constants and the declared template-size/bounding-box/color-count shortcuts. Default grid dimensions were tightened so generated pairs retain the canonical grow-or-reshape profile; factor 1 remains a valid explicit override. Calls now reject unknown/coerced controls, all axes are exactly observable, and generation is deterministic and global-RNG neutral.
+
+Verification retained: 17 focused tests; clean defect lint; a complete fixed-seed census of 12 lessons, 48 query rotations and ten declared rivals with zero ambiguities/warnings/errors (`checks/5a6c8785f6d9-census-v2.summary.json`); and a direct source-bound override contract over 19,620 accepted draws with zero findings (`checks/5a6c8785f6d9-override-direct/`). The managed override controller itself timed out after its child stopped reporting at 4,000 draws, while the same child command completed in 15.01 seconds in the retained runtime closure. These are finite declared-rival checks, not universal uniqueness or owner approval.
